{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123877","id":4651211566,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFTvbLg","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123877","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123877.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123877.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123877","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123877/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123877/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123877/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e078a58f4fae61249df75db788be81ec9f6a6930","number":123877,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Optimize `Mathf.DegToRad`, `Mathf.RadToDeg`, `Mathf.Lerp` in C#","user":{"login":"Joy-less","id":65855333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODU1MzMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65855333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less","html_url":"https://github.com/Joy-less","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nImproves the performance of C#'s `Mathf.DegToRad`, `Mathf.RadToDeg`, and `Mathf.Lerp` functions by using the .NET methods `float.DegreesToRadians`, `float.RadiansToDegrees`, and `float.Lerp` (and the same for `double`).\r\n\r\nThose methods use intrinsics, which seems to make them about 40% faster. They're already very fast, but these methods are used a lot, and `Mathf.Lerp` is also called by methods like `Vector3.Lerp`, so it may be worth doing.\r\n\r\nThis PR will result in a slight change of behaviour with extreme values. For example, the `float.DegreesToRadians` method multiplies first and divides second, which will slightly improve the precision with small values but slightly reduce the precision with massive values. I don't know if the .NET math functions need to exactly match the core C++ math functions.\r\n\r\nBenchmarks (100 million iterations):\r\n```\r\nGodot DegToRad: 298.1016ms\r\n.NET  DegToRad: 188.1239ms\r\nGodot RadToDeg: 302.1955ms\r\n.NET  RadToDeg: 188.4434ms\r\nGodot Lerp: 337.4285ms\r\n.NET  Lerp: 191.9934ms\r\n```\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>See benchmarks source code</summary>\r\n\r\nThese benchmarks benchmark `double`. I did also benchmark `float` and got similar results.\r\n\r\n```cs\r\nusing System.Diagnostics;\r\n\r\npublic class DegRadBench {\r\n    public double Value = 0;\r\n\r\n    public void BenchGodotDegToRad() {\r\n        long s = Stopwatch.GetTimestamp();\r\n        for (int i = 0; i < 100_000_000; i++) {\r\n            Value = Mathf.DegToRad(35.3);\r\n        }\r\n        GD.Print(\"Godot DegToRad: \" + Stopwatch.GetElapsedTime(s).TotalMilliseconds + \"ms\");\r\n    }\r\n    public void BenchDotNetDegToRad() {\r\n        long s = Stopwatch.GetTimestamp();\r\n        for (int i = 0; i < 100_000_000; i++) {\r\n            Value = double.DegreesToRadians(35.3);\r\n        }\r\n        GD.Print(\".NET  DegToRad: \" + Stopwatch.GetElapsedTime(s).TotalMilliseconds + \"ms\");\r\n    }\r\n    public void BenchGodotRadToDeg() {\r\n        long s = Stopwatch.GetTimestamp();\r\n        for (int i = 0; i < 100_000_000; i++) {\r\n            Value = Mathf.RadToDeg(35.3);\r\n        }\r\n        GD.Print(\"Godot RadToDeg: \" + Stopwatch.GetElapsedTime(s).TotalMilliseconds + \"ms\");\r\n    }\r\n    public void BenchDotNetRadToDeg() {\r\n        long s = Stopwatch.GetTimestamp();\r\n        for (int i = 0; i < 100_000_000; i++) {\r\n            Value = double.RadiansToDegrees(35.3);\r\n        }\r\n        GD.Print(\".NET  RadToDeg: \" + Stopwatch.GetElapsedTime(s).TotalMilliseconds + \"ms\");\r\n    }\r\n    public void BenchGodotLerp() {\r\n        long s = Stopwatch.GetTimestamp();\r\n        for (int i = 0; i < 100_000_000; i++) {\r\n            Value = Mathf.Lerp(23.4, 96.2, 0.45);\r\n        }\r\n        GD.Print(\"Godot Lerp: \" + Stopwatch.GetElapsedTime(s).TotalMilliseconds + \"ms\");\r\n    }\r\n    public void BenchDotNetLerp() {\r\n        long s = Stopwatch.GetTimestamp();\r\n        for (int i = 0; i < 100_000_000; i++) {\r\n            Value = double.Lerp(23.4, 96.2, 0.45);\r\n        }\r\n        GD.Print(\".NET  Lerp: \" + Stopwatch.GetElapsedTime(s).TotalMilliseconds + \"ms\");\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\npublic class DegRadBenchRunner {\r\n    private readonly DegRadBench DegRadBench = new();\r\n\r\n    public async void RunLoop() {\r\n        while (true) {\r\n            DegRadBench.BenchGodotDegToRad();\r\n            DegRadBench.BenchDotNetDegToRad();\r\n            DegRadBench.BenchGodotRadToDeg();\r\n            DegRadBench.BenchDotNetRadToDeg();\r\n            DegRadBench.BenchGodotLerp();\r\n            DegRadBench.BenchDotNetLerp();\r\n            GD.Print(\"----------\");\r\n            await Task.Delay(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(1.0));\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nSee also #69490.\r\n\r\nNo AI used.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name"